    "evaluator_feedback": "[DIAGNOSIS]:\nThe error \"The name 'timeoutT' cannot be found\" at line 172 arises because the let-bound variable timeoutT is not in scope where it is referenced in the implication (specifically, in the consequent of the implication at line 172). In Alloy, the scope of a let-binding is limited to the block in which it is defined, and the use of nested braces in this fact means that timeoutT is not available in all branches of the predicate as intended. Previous (rejected) fixes attempted to restructure the let-binding but did not address the underlying scoping issue that results from using nested let-statements versus keeping all logic within a single let block. However, an alternative approach is to inline the definition of timeoutT at its point of use, thus avoiding scope issues entirely.\n\n[FIX INTENT]:\nInline the definition of timeoutT directly at its point of use, removing the let-binding.\n\n[REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS]:\n- Step 1: In fact EmergencyModeDurationAndExit, locate the line:\n  ```\n  let timeoutT = TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]] |\n  ```\n  Remove this let-binding entirely.\n- Step 2: Replace all occurrences of the variable timeoutT within this fact with its explicit definition, i.e., TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]].\n- Step 3: For example, change:\n  ```\n  TO/lte[et.endedAt, timeoutT]\n  ```\n  to\n  ```\n  TO/lte[et.endedAt, TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[TO/next[start]]]]]]\n  ```\n  and similarly for other references (such as in the \"some timeoutT and ...\" line).\n- Step 4: Remove any references to timeoutT, as it is inlined.\n\n[RATIONALE]:\nThis fix is Alloy 6 compliant because it eliminates scoping problems by inlining the value wherever it is used, rather than relying on let-bindings whose scope may be unintentionally limited by braces or block structure—a strategy not previously attempted.\n\n[LESSON]:\nInlining expressions in Alloy avoids scoping pitfalls with let-bound variables, especially in complex nested or multi-branch facts.",
