    "evaluator_feedback": "[DIAGNOSIS]:\nThe error occurs at line 242 in pred R1R2R3, specifically at the assignment s.emergencyAdmins = (some et: EmergencyTrigger | TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt]).admins. The problem is that (some et: EmergencyTrigger | ...) is a Boolean expression (PrimitiveBoolean), not a set or relation. The attempted use of .admins after a Boolean is invalid in Alloy. Previous fixes focused on scoping, let-bindings, and operator replacements, but did not address this fundamental misuse of the comprehension result.\n\n[FIX INTENT]:\nReplace the Boolean-valued set comprehension with a proper set-producing expression that yields the set of admins from active EmergencyTrigger(s) at time s.t.\n\n[REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS]:\n- Step 1: In pred R1R2R3, locate the line:\n      s.emergencyAdmins = \n          (some et: EmergencyTrigger |\n              TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt]\n          ).admins\n- Step 2: Replace it with:\n      s.emergencyAdmins = \n          { et: EmergencyTrigger | TO/lte[et.at, s.t] and TO/lt[s.t, et.endedAt] }.admins\n  This uses a set comprehension (curly braces) to produce the set of EmergencyTrigger(s) active at s.t, and then collects their admins.\n\n[RATIONALE]:\nThis fix uses Alloy's set comprehension (not a Boolean quantifier) to yield a set of EmergencyTrigger(s), allowing the .admins field to be accessed as a set of Administrator(s); this approach is syntactically valid in Alloy 6 and was not attempted in prior fixes.\n\n[LESSON]:\nWhen you need to derive a set from a condition in Alloy, use set comprehension with curly braces, not quantifiers that return Booleans.",
