djust assertions and test scenarios to match clarified semantics.\n**MANDATORY**: Do not attempt further model-level repairs until the above requirement updates are completed and reflected in the model.\n\n\n\n--- Diagnostic Experiments (verbatim from InterpretResults, auto-included) ---\n1. Relax the revocation constraint to allow Emergency-mode delegations to persist into the first Normal state, rerun DelegationCoverage—does it become SAT?\n2. Split DelegationCoverage into two independent predicates (already in model)—run each independently to confirm which is UNSAT.\n3. Add a scenario predicate that witnesses an Emergency-mode delegation, then its revocation, then a Normal-mode delegation—does this produce a satisfying instance, or is this sequence blocked?\n4. Temporarily weaken assertR3_OnlyTriggeringAdminsGetEmergencyPrivs to allow privilege assignment errors for one step at Emergency end—does the assertion pass?\n5. Ask user to clarify witness requirement (see BLOCKING QUESTIONS).\n=== POTENTIAL REQUIREMENT ISSUES ===\n- Issue type: requirement ambiguity (resolved by user)\n  - Issue: R8.1 (DelegationCoverage) previously unclear on whether both delegation types must be present in the same execution.\n  - Rationale: User clarified existential semantics; requirement and model must be updated for this.\n  - Action: Update R8.1 and model to require existence of Emergency-mode and Normal-mode delegations in possible (not necessarily the same) executions.\n\n- Issue type: requirement inconsistency (resolved by user)\n  - Issue: R4.2 (delegation revocation timing) was ambiguous about whether Emergency-mode delegations could persist into Normal.\n  - Rationale: User clarified strict revocation required; update wording and model logic.\n  - Action: Update R4.2 and model to explicitly prohibit Emergency-initiated delegations persisting into Normal mode.\n\n- Issue type: requirement ambiguity (resolved by user)\n  - Issue: R3.3 (emergency privilege assignment) did not specify exclusivity at all times.\n  - Rationale: User clarified exclusivity must be strict and always enforced.\n  - Action: Update R3.3 and corresponding assertions to strictly prohibit privilege handoff or overlap.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\nNone - assumptions appear sound\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: R8.1 (DelegationCoverage Verification)\n  - Issue Type: ambiguity (now resolved)\n  - Evidence: Model UNSAT and user clarification indicate existential coverage suffices.\n  - Recommended Update: \"For verification, it is sufficient that there exist executions in which at least one delegation occurs during Emergency mode and (separately) at least one occurs during Normal mode; presence in the same execution is not required.\"\n  - Implication: Removes contradiction with revocation timing; allows independent coverage.\n\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: R4.2 (Emergency-mode Delegation Revocation)\n  - Issue Type: inconsistency (now resolved)\n  - Evidence: Model and user confirm revocation timing must be strict.\n  - Recommended Update: \"All delegations started during Emergency mode must be revoked by the Emergency/Normal transition; none may persist into any Normal mode state.\"\n  - Implication: Aligns model and requirement; enables satisfiability.\n\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: R3.3 (Emergency Privileges Assignment)\n  - Issue Type: ambiguity (now resolved)\n  - Evidence: Counterexamples and user clarification indicate only triggering admins may ever hold emergency privileges.\n  - Recommended Update: \"Only the two administrators who triggered Emergency mode may ever hold emergency privileges at any time, including during transitions; strictly forbidden for any other administrator.\"\n  - Implication: Removes ambiguity and aligns verification with intended exclusivity.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nQ49_1: confirmed – User clarified R8.1 as existential, not per-execution.\nQ49_2: confirmed – User clarified R4.2 requires strict revocation at transition.\nQ43_3: confirmed – User clarified emergency privilege exclusivity.\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Update requirements and model per user-clarified semantics for R8.1 (existential coverage), R4.2 (strict revocation timing), and R3.3 (emergency privilege exclusivity).\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- Adjust model predicates, assertions, and tests to reflect updated requirements.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- After requirement and model updates, add explicit negative and edge case tests for delegation and privilege transitions at mode boundaries.\n```",
